# LiveRamp

LiveRamp is a global technology company and the leader in data collaboration. LiveRamp's data collaboration network connects every signal, agent, surface, and channel to fuel AI-powered marketing that drives exponentially better performance — grounded in trust.

LiveRamp helps marketers build enduring brand and business value by driving better performance with AI. The platform brings fragmented data together so teams can see what's working, move faster, and improve returns without extra complexity. Marketers can plan, run, measure, and optimize campaigns more easily and effectively, and gain a deeper understanding of their customers — with built-in privacy and security protections ensuring data is handled responsibly at every step.

## How LiveRamp Works
Understanding LiveRamp means understanding how raw data becomes resolved identities, activated audiences, and measurable outcomes.

Start with identity. A brand uploads its first-party data, securely and with appropriate permissions (LiveRamp processes 10 petabytes of data every day, equivalent to about five trillion pages). That data is resolved to RampID, a secure, durable identifier that accurately links and translates any authenticated identifier or combination of identifiers while respecting each party’s privacy rules. RampID is the connective tissue of the LiveRamp network. It doesn't replace your enterprise identity; it translates across partners and platforms so your data stays addressable without exposing personally identifiable information.

LiveRamp is cloud-first by design. Its capabilities are embedded directly within AWS, Google Cloud, Snowflake, and Databricks – which means your data doesn’t need to move. LiveRamp brings the technology to your data, not the other way around.
From that foundation, three core use cases drive how marketers put LiveRamp to work.

1. Consumer Insights. LiveRamp helps you build a connected view of your customers across systems and identifiers, enrich profiles with trusted data from the LiveRamp Data Marketplace, develop scalable prospect audiences for acquisition and growth, and power personalization strategies with unified identity. With LiveRamp, fragmented data becomes a complete, actionable picture of who your customers are and what drives their decisions.

2. Planning & Activation. With identity resolved, you can reach and activate audiences across platforms and channels, expand targeting through lookalike modeling, monetize data assets through the Marketplace, and collaborate with partners to identify audience overlap and co-marketing opportunities. LiveRamp connects resolved data to 650+ partner destinations, so activation happens wherever your customers spend time, without depending on third-party cookies.

3. Measurement & Optimization. LiveRamp enables you to measure marketing performance across platforms and channels, quantify lift and incrementality, and continuously improve campaign outcomes using conversion and engagement signals. Data clean rooms – secure environments with built-in governance controls – let two or more parties analyze overlapping data without any side seeing another's raw records. A data clean room is how a CPG brand and a retailer measure campaign performance together. It's how a publisher and an advertiser prove media value without data leaving its source. With AI-driven optimization built in, teams can automate decisioning and close the loop from insight to action in real time.


